---
// Privacy: what nepdate.com and patro.nepdate.com store and send. Kept in step with the code: the
// Content-Security-Policy in public/_headers, the localStorage keys in web/ and patro/, and
// ADR-0005's no-tracking rule.
import InfoPage from "../components/InfoPage.astro";
import { HUB, PATRO } from "../data/ports";

const description =
  "NepDate's privacy notice: no accounts, cookies, analytics or advertising on nepdate.com and patro.nepdate.com, and what the apps and libraries do with your data.";
const site = Astro.site?.href ?? "https://nepdate.com/";
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Privacy",
  url: new URL("/privacy/", site).href,
  description,
  about: { "@id": `${site}#org` },
};
---

<InfoPage title="Privacy | NepDate" heading="Privacy" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <p class="info-lede">
    nepdate.com and <a href={PATRO}>patro.nepdate.com</a> have no accounts, no cookies, no analytics and no advertising.
    Nothing you do on them is collected by NepDate.
  </p>

  <h2>What the websites keep in your browser</h2>
  <p>A few settings stay in your browser's local storage, on your device only, and are never sent anywhere:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your light or dark theme (<code>starlight-theme</code>);</li>
    <li>whether the web fonts have loaded once, so the next page shows them sooner;</li>
    <li>on the patro, whether you read it in Nepali or English (<code>patro-lang</code>).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Clearing the site's data in your browser removes them. The date converter and the search run in your browser too.</p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    Both sites are static pages served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare handles your IP address and request
    details to deliver the pages and protect them from abuse, under the{" "}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>. NepDate does not turn on request
    logging. The pages load no scripts, fonts or images from other sites; their Content-Security-Policy allows only the
    site's own files.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to GitHub</h2>
  <p>
    Reporting a wrong date, asking a question and reading the source all happen on GitHub. What you write there is
    public and is covered by the GitHub privacy statement, not by this page.
  </p>

  <h2>The apps and libraries</h2>
  <p>
    MitiBar sends nothing about you anywhere. It connects to the internet only when you press Check for updates, or,
    if you turn on automatic checks, when Settings opens, at most once a day, and then asks GitHub only for the latest
    version number. The NepDate libraries run inside your own
    program, read only the calendar data they ship with, and make no network requests either.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If any of this changes, for example if a site starts counting visits, this page changes first, in a public pull
    request in the <a href={HUB}>hub repository</a>. Questions go through <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.
  </p>
</InfoPage>
